("AI, ML & deep learning","Basic",["AI is broad; ML learns from data; deep learning uses neural networks","Training updates weights; inference uses weights","Model, tokenizer and dataset have distinct versions"],"Task quality and dataset coverage","Accuracy = correct predictions / examples, when suitable","A support chatbot generates text using an existing model and retrieved context.",[("Does an inference prompt train weights?","Normally no. Training is a separate operation."),("Why pin the tokenizer?","It changes token counts and sometimes compatibility or output.")],["PyTorch inference"]),
